# /wordnew API — mock ⇄ real, one TYPE, one switch

Spec: `docs/WORDNEW_API_MOCK_PATTERN.md`; contract: `apps/wordnew/api/README.md`.

- One TYPE surface: all models + `WfNewApi` live in `api/WfNewApiTypes.ts`; `WfNewTypes.ts`/`WfNewMockDb.ts` re-export, never redefine.
- Two impls, same contract: `WfNewApiMock` (offline) and `WfNewApiHttp` (delegates to `wordflowApi`).
- One switch: consumers `import { wfNewApi } from '../api'`; `api/index.ts` is the ONLY mock-vs-real choice. Exactly one active import + one active `export const wfNewApi` (toggle the pair together). Default=http; offline/AI-Studio=mock.
- Change the API ⇒ sync types + both impls + `WfNewMockDb` together; mock returns exact backend shape.
- No silent gaps: missing endpoint ⇒ http serves curated data + logs once, never fake success.
- Endpoints in `WfNewEndpoints.ts` (modeled on `WordflowApiManager`): default `:9000` list, STORED-FIRST auto-select, `/api/health` probe, offline retry. Never hardcode a base URL.
- Use shared `core/`: `core/persistence` (StorageManager/StorageKeys), `useSyncExternalStore` store pattern (`useWfNewEndpoints`), `core/notify` toasts, `Portal`+`OVERLAY_Z` for dialogs (no raw `fixed inset-0 z-50`).
- English only.
